      "solution": "n = int(input())\nl = int(input())\n\nrep = str(n)+\",\"+str(n)\na = n\nb = n\nwhile len(rep)<l+1:\n    c = a+b\n    rep+=str(c)\n    if c < 10:\n        a=b\n        b=c\n    elif c > 9:\n        d = str(c)\n        a = int(d[0])\n        b = int(d[1])\n\nif len(rep) == l+2:\n    print(rep[:-1])\nelse:\n    print(rep)\n",
      "statement": "Create your own <<Fibonacci sequence>> from a given number [[n]], and of length [[l]].\n\nTips : \n\nThe Fibonacci sequence is built like this :\n\nA,BCD...\nB = A + 0\nC = A + B\nD = B + C\n\nIf B + C = 12, D = 1 and E = 2\nExemple : 1,12358<<13>>4     (5+8 = <<13>>) ; (1+3 = 4)",
