    "statementHTML": "<div class=\"statement-body\">\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-goal\">\n   <h2><span class=\"icon icon-goal\">&nbsp;</span><span>Goal </span></h2>\n   <span class=\"question-statement\">Create your own <strong>Fibonacci sequence</strong> from a given number <var>n</var>, and of length <var>l</var>.<br><br>Tips : <br><br>The Fibonacci sequence is built like this :<br><br>A,BCD...<br>B = A + 0<br>C = A + B<br>D = B + C<br><br>If B + C = 12, D = 1 and E = 2<br>Exemple : 1,12358<strong>13</strong>4     (5+8 = <strong>13</strong>) ; (1+3 = 4)</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-protocol\">\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-input\"><strong>Line 1</strong> An integer <var>n</var> that is the starting number of your Fibonacci sequence<br><strong>Line 2</strong> An integer <var>l</var> that is the length demanded of your Fibonacci sequence</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-output\"><strong>Line 1</strong> A string representing your Fibonacci sequence</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Constraints</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-constraints\">0 &le; <var>n</var> &le; 9<br>2 &le; <var>l</var> &le; 1000</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Example</div>\n      <div class=\"statement-inout\">\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-in\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-in\">1\n5</pre>\n         </div>\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-out\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-out\">1,1235</pre>\n         </div>\n      </div>\n   </div>\n</div>"
